Package: kicad-dbgsym
Version: @VERSION@
Section: debug
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: kicad (= @VERSION@)
Auto-Built-Package: debug-symbols
Maintainer: Pete Dietl <petedietl@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://www.kicad.org
Description: debug symbols for kicad
 Debug info for the binaries in the kicad package, separated out at build
 time and indexed by build ID under /usr/lib/debug/.build-id.
 .
 gdb searches /usr/lib/debug by default, so installing this package is all
 that is needed to turn addresses in a backtrace into function names, source
 files and line numbers. Nothing needs configuring, and the kicad package
 itself is byte-for-byte the same whether this is installed or not.
 .
 Only useful when reporting or investigating a crash or a hang. It is far
 larger than the package it describes.
